From 8a9e9db32420948818bf89410ad30c087ad20086 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "huimin.he" <huimin.he@cybertan.com.tw>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: add power limit table for sonicfi_rap736c

Add the 2.4G and 5G part of Griffin_Power_limit_table_2026_1005_RAP736C.xlsx
to the RAP736C DTS as a power-limits node, without regdomain/country so
mt76 uses it for every country:
- rates-*: the rate table (SKU_OUT sheet)
- paths-*: the per-path backoff table (Back_off_OUT sheet)
The 6G part of the table is not used. The CCK entries on 5G are
dropped (the Ch130 row of the sheet has 127 there).

The table sets every 2.4G and 5G rate limit to 30 dBm and keeps the
real limits in the backoff table, so mt76 has to support both:
- mt76: parse "rates-eht" from DT; mt76_get_rate_power_limits() never
  filled the EHT limits, so EHT rates used the unrestricted target
  power.
- mt76: mt7996: send the path table to the firmware and enable the SKU
  and backoff limits, based on the MediaTek SDK patch "mtk: mt76:
  mt7996: support txpower backoff table". It changes the paths-* DT
  format to the connac3 layout.
- mt76: cap the rate and backoff entries by the total power of the
  configured chains on connac3; the firmware takes them as total power,
  and the per-chain cap left 5G up to 4.5 dB below the table.

Both mt76 patches (3000, 3001) go to patches-sonicfi_rap736c, so other
boards are not affected.

Signed-off-by: huimin.he <huimin.he@cybertan.com.tw>
---
 ...-parse-EHT-rate-power-limits-from-DT.patch |   40 +
 ...mt7996-support-txpower-backoff-table.patch |  313 ++++
 .../mediatek/dts/mt7987a-sonicfi-rap736c.dts  | 1272 +++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 1625 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 package/kernel/mt76/patches-sonicfi_rap736c/3001-mt76-parse-EHT-rate-power-limits-from-DT.patch
 create mode 100644 package/kernel/mt76/patches-sonicfi_rap736c/3002-mt76-mt7996-support-txpower-backoff-table.patch

diff --git a/package/kernel/mt76/patches-sonicfi_rap736c/3001-mt76-parse-EHT-rate-power-limits-from-DT.patch b/package/kernel/mt76/patches-sonicfi_rap736c/3001-mt76-parse-EHT-rate-power-limits-from-DT.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..5a5924e606
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mt76/patches-sonicfi_rap736c/3001-mt76-parse-EHT-rate-power-limits-from-DT.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+From 4a37df45d7d598c9ba487013a6c9c5b3f43b13d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: "huimin.he" <huimin.he@cybertan.com.tw>
+Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:30:00 +0800
+Subject: [PATCH] mt76: parse EHT rate power limits from DT
+
+struct mt76_power_limits has an eht[16][16] table and mt7996 sends it
+to the firmware with the rest of the SKU table, but
+mt76_get_rate_power_limits() never fills it from the device tree, so
+EHT rates always use the unrestricted target power.
+
+Add a "rates-eht" property, using the same format as "rates-ru":
+each entry is <count mcs0 ... mcs15> and applies to the next <count>
+RU/MRU sizes, in firmware order: RU26, RU52, RU106, RU242, RU484,
+RU996, RU2x996, RU4x996, RU52+26, RU106+26, RU484+242, RU996+484,
+RU996+484+242, RU2x996+484, RU3x996, RU3x996+484.
+
+Signed-off-by: huimin.he <huimin.he@cybertan.com.tw>
+---
+ eeprom.c | 5 +++++
+ 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)
+
+diff --git a/eeprom.c b/eeprom.c
+index 28dbda6..413a677 100644
+--- a/eeprom.c
++++ b/eeprom.c
+@@ -511,6 +511,11 @@ s8 mt76_get_rate_power_limits(struct mt76_phy *phy,
+ 				     ARRAY_SIZE(dest->ru), val, len, target_power,
+ 				     txs_delta, &max_power, n_chains, MT76_SKU_RATE);
+ 
++	val = mt76_get_of_array_s8(np, "rates-eht", &len, ARRAY_SIZE(dest->eht[0]) + 1);
++	mt76_apply_multi_array_limit(dev, dest->eht[0], ARRAY_SIZE(dest->eht[0]),
++				     ARRAY_SIZE(dest->eht), val, len, target_power,
++				     txs_delta, &max_power, n_chains, MT76_SKU_RATE);
++
+ 	val = mt76_get_of_array_s8(np, "paths-cck", &len, ARRAY_SIZE(dest->path.cck));
+ 	mt76_apply_array_limit(dev, dest->path.cck, ARRAY_SIZE(dest->path.cck), val,
+ 			       target_power, txs_delta, &max_power, n_chains, MT76_SKU_BACKOFF);
+-- 
+2.34.1
+
diff --git a/package/kernel/mt76/patches-sonicfi_rap736c/3002-mt76-mt7996-support-txpower-backoff-table.patch b/package/kernel/mt76/patches-sonicfi_rap736c/3002-mt76-mt7996-support-txpower-backoff-table.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..1d90654f2e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mt76/patches-sonicfi_rap736c/3002-mt76-mt7996-support-txpower-backoff-table.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,313 @@
+From 3b38c635032c5bf4f91ab60010d948d1aa7437f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: "huimin.he" <huimin.he@cybertan.com.tw>
+Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0800
+Subject: [PATCH] mt76: mt7996: support txpower backoff table
+
+The RAP736C power limit table keeps the real limits in the per-path
+(backoff) table, but mt7996 only sends the rate table to the firmware
+and never enables the SKU or backoff limits, so the table has no
+effect.
+
+Based on the MediaTek SDK patch "mtk: mt76: mt7996: support txpower
+backoff table":
+- grow mt76_power_limits.path to the connac3 layout: 5 CCK/OFDM
+  entries and 16 RU groups of 15 stream combinations (1T1ss..5T5ss),
+  read from the paths-* DT properties.
+- send the path table (TX_POWER_LIMIT_TABLE_PATH) after the rate table
+  when the DT has one for the channel.
+- enable the SKU limit and, when a path table is used, the backoff
+  limit in the firmware.
+- mt7915 sends the same number of path entries as before.
+
+The connac3 firmware takes the rate and backoff entries as total power
+(5G ch36 BW80: backoff entry 30 -> 15.5 dBm measured on 3 chains, rate
+readback 32 at EHT MCS13 -> 16.6 dBm measured), but
+mt76_apply_array_limit() capped them to per-chain power: with a 23 dBm
+txpower on 3 chains, rates to 2 * 23 - 9 = 37 (18.5 dBm) and backoff
+3T2S to 37, so 5G stayed up to 4.5 dB below the table. On connac3, cap
+all entries by the total power of the configured chains instead, and
+fill rate entries missing in DT with the total power. The returned max
+power stays per-chain.
+
+Signed-off-by: huimin.he <huimin.he@cybertan.com.tw>
+---
+ eeprom.c     |  27 +++++++++++--
+ mt76.h       |   8 ++--
+ mt7915/mcu.c |  14 +++----
+ mt7996/mcu.c | 105 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
+ mt7996/mcu.h |   2 +
+ 5 files changed, 127 insertions(+), 29 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/eeprom.c b/eeprom.c
+index 413a677..33a21b1 100644
+--- a/eeprom.c
++++ b/eeprom.c
+@@ -360,7 +360,7 @@ mt76_apply_array_limit(struct mt76_dev *dev, s8 *pwr, size_t pwr_len,
+ 		u8 backoff_chain_idx = i;
+ 		int backoff_n_chains;
+ 		s8 backoff_delta;
+-		s8 delta;
++		s8 delta, cur;
+ 
+ 		switch (type) {
+ 		case MT76_SKU_RATE:
+@@ -380,7 +380,21 @@ mt76_apply_array_limit(struct mt76_dev *dev, s8 *pwr, size_t pwr_len,
+ 			return;
+ 		}
+ 
+-		pwr[i] = min_t(s8, target_power + delta - backoff_delta, data[i] + nss_delta);
++		if (is_mt799x(dev)) {
++			/* connac3 firmware takes rate and backoff entries as
++			 * total power, so limit them by the total power of the
++			 * configured chains instead of the per-chain power.
++			 * max_power stays per-chain.
++			 */
++			delta = mt76_tx_power_path_delta(n_chains);
++			pwr[i] = min_t(int, target_power + delta,
++				       data[i] + nss_delta);
++			cur = pwr[i] - delta;
++		} else {
++			pwr[i] = min_t(s8, target_power + delta - backoff_delta,
++				       data[i] + nss_delta);
++			cur = pwr[i];
++		}
+ 
+ 		/* used for padding, doesn't need to be considered */
+ 		if (data[i] >= S8_MAX - 1)
+@@ -390,7 +404,7 @@ mt76_apply_array_limit(struct mt76_dev *dev, s8 *pwr, size_t pwr_len,
+ 		if (type != MT76_SKU_RATE && n_chains != backoff_n_chains)
+ 			continue;
+ 
+-		*max_power = max(*max_power, pwr[i]);
++		*max_power = max(*max_power, cur);
+ 	}
+ }
+ 
+@@ -458,7 +472,12 @@ s8 mt76_get_rate_power_limits(struct mt76_phy *phy,
+ 	s8 txs_delta;
+ 	int n_chains = hweight16(phy->chainmask);
+ 
+-	memset(dest, target_power, sizeof(*dest) - sizeof(dest->path));
++	/* rate entries missing in DT: no limit below the txpower, which is
++	 * total power on connac3
++	 */
++	memset(dest, is_mt799x(dev) ?
++	       target_power + mt76_tx_power_path_delta(n_chains) : target_power,
++	       sizeof(*dest) - sizeof(dest->path));
+ 	memset(&dest->path, 0, sizeof(dest->path));
+ 
+ 	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_OF))
+diff --git a/mt76.h b/mt76.h
+index 273f38e..186a251 100644
+--- a/mt76.h
++++ b/mt76.h
+@@ -1154,11 +1154,11 @@ struct mt76_power_limits {
+ 	s8 eht[16][16];
+ 
+ 	struct {
+-		s8 cck[4];
+-		s8 ofdm[4];
++		s8 cck[5];
++		s8 ofdm[5];
+ 		s8 ofdm_bf[4];
+-		s8 ru[7][10];
+-		s8 ru_bf[7][10];
++		s8 ru[16][15];
++		s8 ru_bf[16][15];
+ 	} path;
+ };
+ 
+diff --git a/mt7915/mcu.c b/mt7915/mcu.c
+index c9567aa..b97e1a2 100644
+--- a/mt7915/mcu.c
++++ b/mt7915/mcu.c
+@@ -3484,15 +3484,15 @@ int mt7915_mcu_set_txpower_sku(struct mt7915_phy *phy)
+ 
+ 	hdr.limit_type = TX_POWER_LIMIT_TABLE_PATH;
+ 	skb_put_data(skb, &hdr, sizeof(hdr));
+-	skb_put_data(skb, &la.path.cck, sizeof(la.path.cck));
+-	skb_put_data(skb, &la.path.ofdm, sizeof(la.path.ofdm));
+-	skb_put_data(skb, &la.path.ofdm_bf[1], sizeof(la.path.ofdm_bf) - 1);
++	skb_put_data(skb, &la.path.cck, 4);
++	skb_put_data(skb, &la.path.ofdm, 4);
++	skb_put_data(skb, &la.path.ofdm_bf[1], 3);
+ 
+ 	/* HT20 and HT40 */
+-	skb_put_data(skb, &la.path.ru[3], sizeof(la.path.ru[3]));
+-	skb_put_data(skb, &la.path.ru_bf[3][1], sizeof(la.path.ru_bf[3]) - 1);
+-	skb_put_data(skb, &la.path.ru[4], sizeof(la.path.ru[4]));
+-	skb_put_data(skb, &la.path.ru_bf[4][1], sizeof(la.path.ru_bf[4]) - 1);
++	skb_put_data(skb, &la.path.ru[3], 10);
++	skb_put_data(skb, &la.path.ru_bf[3][1], 9);
++	skb_put_data(skb, &la.path.ru[4], 10);
++	skb_put_data(skb, &la.path.ru_bf[4][1], 9);
+ 
+ 	/* start from non-bf and bf fields of
+ 	 * BW20/RU242, BW40/RU484, BW80/RU996, BW160/RU2x996,
+diff --git a/mt7996/mcu.c b/mt7996/mcu.c
+index d664767..bdd41e7 100644
+--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
++++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
+@@ -5254,9 +5254,36 @@ int mt7996_mcu_set_sniffer_mode(struct mt7996_phy *phy, bool enabled)
+ 				 sizeof(req), true);
+ }
+ 
++static int
++mt7996_mcu_set_tx_power_ctrl(struct mt7996_phy *phy, u8 power_ctrl_id,
++			     bool enable)
++{
++	struct {
++		u8 _rsv[4];
++
++		__le16 tag;
++		__le16 len;
++
++		u8 power_ctrl_id;
++		u8 enable;
++		u8 band_idx;
++		u8 rsv[1];
++	} __packed req = {
++		.tag = cpu_to_le16(power_ctrl_id),
++		.len = cpu_to_le16(sizeof(req) - 4),
++		.power_ctrl_id = power_ctrl_id,
++		.enable = enable,
++		.band_idx = phy->mt76->band_idx,
++	};
++
++	return mt76_mcu_send_msg(&phy->dev->mt76, MCU_WM_UNI_CMD(TXPOWER),
++				 &req, sizeof(req), false);
++}
++
+ int mt7996_mcu_set_txpower_sku(struct mt7996_phy *phy)
+ {
+ #define TX_POWER_LIMIT_TABLE_RATE	0
++#define TX_POWER_LIMIT_TABLE_PATH	1
+ 	struct mt7996_dev *dev = phy->dev;
+ 	struct mt76_phy *mphy = phy->mt76;
+ 	struct tx_power_limit_table_ctrl {
+@@ -5274,45 +5301,95 @@ int mt7996_mcu_set_txpower_sku(struct mt7996_phy *phy)
+ 		.power_limit_type = TX_POWER_LIMIT_TABLE_RATE,
+ 		.band_idx = phy->mt76->band_idx,
+ 	};
+-	struct mt76_power_limits la = {};
++	struct mt76_power_limits *la;
+ 	struct sk_buff *skb;
+-	int i, tx_power;
++	int i, ret, tx_power;
++	bool path_en;
++
++	la = kzalloc(sizeof(*la), GFP_KERNEL);
++	if (!la)
++		return -ENOMEM;
+ 
+ 	tx_power = mt76_get_power_bound(mphy, phy->txpower);
+ 	tx_power = mt76_get_rate_power_limits(mphy, mphy->chandef.chan,
+-					      &la, tx_power);
++					      la, tx_power);
+ 	mphy->txpower_cur = tx_power;
+ 
++	/* per-path (backoff) limits are only valid when they are set in DT */
++	path_en = !!la->path.ofdm[0];
++
++	ret = mt7996_mcu_set_tx_power_ctrl(phy, UNI_TXPOWER_SKU_POWER_LIMIT_CTRL,
++					   true);
++	if (ret)
++		goto out;
++
++	ret = mt7996_mcu_set_tx_power_ctrl(phy, UNI_TXPOWER_BACKOFF_POWER_LIMIT_CTRL,
++					   path_en);
++	if (ret)
++		goto out;
++
+ 	skb = mt76_mcu_msg_alloc(&dev->mt76, NULL,
+ 				 sizeof(req) + MT7996_SKU_PATH_NUM);
+-	if (!skb)
+-		return -ENOMEM;
++	if (!skb) {
++		ret = -ENOMEM;
++		goto out;
++	}
+ 
+ 	skb_put_data(skb, &req, sizeof(req));
+ 	/* cck and ofdm */
+-	skb_put_data(skb, &la.cck, sizeof(la.cck));
+-	skb_put_data(skb, &la.ofdm, sizeof(la.ofdm));
++	skb_put_data(skb, &la->cck, sizeof(la->cck));
++	skb_put_data(skb, &la->ofdm, sizeof(la->ofdm));
+ 	/* ht20 */
+-	skb_put_data(skb, &la.mcs[0], 8);
++	skb_put_data(skb, &la->mcs[0], 8);
+ 	/* ht40 */
+-	skb_put_data(skb, &la.mcs[1], 9);
++	skb_put_data(skb, &la->mcs[1], 9);
+ 
+ 	/* vht */
+ 	for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
+-		skb_put_data(skb, &la.mcs[i], sizeof(la.mcs[i]));
++		skb_put_data(skb, &la->mcs[i], sizeof(la->mcs[i]));
+ 		skb_put_zero(skb, 2);  /* padding */
+ 	}
+ 
+ 	/* he */
+-	skb_put_data(skb, &la.ru[0], sizeof(la.ru));
++	skb_put_data(skb, &la->ru[0], sizeof(la->ru));
+ 	/* eht */
+-	skb_put_data(skb, &la.eht[0], sizeof(la.eht));
++	skb_put_data(skb, &la->eht[0], sizeof(la->eht));
+ 
+ 	/* padding */
+ 	skb_put_zero(skb, MT7996_SKU_PATH_NUM - MT7996_SKU_RATE_NUM);
+ 
+-	return mt76_mcu_skb_send_msg(&dev->mt76, skb,
+-				     MCU_WM_UNI_CMD(TXPOWER), true);
++	ret = mt76_mcu_skb_send_msg(&dev->mt76, skb,
++				    MCU_WM_UNI_CMD(TXPOWER), true);
++	if (ret || !path_en)
++		goto out;
++
++	skb = mt76_mcu_msg_alloc(&dev->mt76, NULL,
++				 sizeof(req) + MT7996_SKU_PATH_NUM);
++	if (!skb) {
++		ret = -ENOMEM;
++		goto out;
++	}
++
++	req.power_limit_type = TX_POWER_LIMIT_TABLE_PATH;
++	skb_put_data(skb, &req, sizeof(req));
++	skb_put_data(skb, &la->path.cck, sizeof(la->path.cck));
++	skb_put_data(skb, &la->path.ofdm, sizeof(la->path.ofdm));
++	skb_put_data(skb, &la->path.ofdm_bf, sizeof(la->path.ofdm_bf));
++
++	/* non-bf and bf fields of RU26, RU52, RU52+26, RU106, RU106+26,
++	 * RU242, RU484, RU484+242, RU996, RU996+484, RU996+484+242,
++	 * RU2x996, RU2x996+484, RU3x996, RU3x996+484 and RU4x996
++	 */
++	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(la->path.ru); i++) {
++		skb_put_data(skb, la->path.ru[i], sizeof(la->path.ru[i]));
++		skb_put_data(skb, la->path.ru_bf[i], sizeof(la->path.ru_bf[i]));
++	}
++
++	ret = mt76_mcu_skb_send_msg(&dev->mt76, skb,
++				    MCU_WM_UNI_CMD(TXPOWER), true);
++out:
++	kfree(la);
++	return ret;
+ }
+ 
+ int mt7996_mcu_cp_support(struct mt7996_dev *dev, u8 mode)
+diff --git a/mt7996/mcu.h b/mt7996/mcu.h
+index 39df136..9e00988 100644
+--- a/mt7996/mcu.h
++++ b/mt7996/mcu.h
+@@ -963,6 +963,8 @@ enum {
+ };
+ 
+ enum {
++	UNI_TXPOWER_SKU_POWER_LIMIT_CTRL = 0,
++	UNI_TXPOWER_BACKOFF_POWER_LIMIT_CTRL = 3,
+ 	UNI_TXPOWER_POWER_LIMIT_TABLE_CTRL = 4,
+ };
+ 
+-- 
+2.34.1
+
diff --git a/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987a-sonicfi-rap736c.dts b/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987a-sonicfi-rap736c.dts
index 0527f0b7f8..d6a60b4b69 100644
--- a/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987a-sonicfi-rap736c.dts
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987a-sonicfi-rap736c.dts
@@ -122,6 +122,1278 @@
 
 			nvmem-cells = <&eeprom_factory>;
 			nvmem-cell-names = "eeprom";
+
+			power-limits {
+				/* Griffin_Power_limit_table_2026_1005_RAP736C.xlsx
+				 * rates-*: SKU_OUT, paths-*: Back_off_OUT, unit 0.5 dBm
+				 */
+				r0 {
+					txpower-2g {
+						r0 {
+							channels = <1 1>;
+							rates-cck = /bits/ 8 <60 60 60 60>;
+							rates-ofdm = /bits/ 8 <60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60>;
+							rates-mcs =
+								/bits/ 8 <2 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60>;
+							rates-ru =
+								/bits/ 8 <5 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60>;
+							rates-eht =
+								/bits/ 8 <5 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60>,
+								/bits/ 8 <3 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126>,
+								/bits/ 8 <2 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60>;
+							paths-cck = /bits/ 8 <48 42 42 42 42>;
+							paths-ofdm = /bits/ 8 <40 34 34 34 34>;
+							paths-ofdm-bf = /bits/ 8 <34 34 34 34>;
+							paths-ru =
+								/bits/ 8 <7 40 34 34 34 34 34 34 34 34 34 34 34 34 34 34>;
+							paths-ru-bf =
+								/bits/ 8 <7 40 34 34 34 34 34 34 34 34 34 34 34 34 34 34>;
+						};
+						r1 {
+							channels = <2 10>;
+							rates-cck = /bits/ 8 <60 60 60 60>;
+							rates-ofdm = /bits/ 8 <60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60>;
+							rates-mcs =
+								/bits/ 8 <2 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60>;
+							rates-ru =
+								/bits/ 8 <5 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60>;
+							rates-eht =
+								/bits/ 8 <5 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60>,
+								/bits/ 8 <3 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126>,
+								/bits/ 8 <2 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60>;
+							paths-cck = /bits/ 8 <48 44 44 44 44>;
+							paths-ofdm = /bits/ 8 <44 38 38 38 38>;
+							paths-ofdm-bf = /bits/ 8 <38 38 38 38>;
+							paths-ru =
+								/bits/ 8 <7 44 38 38 38 38 38 38 38 38 38 38 38 38 38 38>;
+							paths-ru-bf =
+								/bits/ 8 <7 44 38 38 38 38 38 38 38 38 38 38 38 38 38 38>;
+						};
+						r2 {
+							channels = <11 14>;
+							rates-cck = /bits/ 8 <60 60 60 60>;
+							rates-ofdm = /bits/ 8 <60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60>;
+							rates-mcs =
+								/bits/ 8 <2 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60>;
+							rates-ru =
+								/bits/ 8 <5 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60>;
+							rates-eht =
+								/bits/ 8 <5 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60>,
+								/bits/ 8 <3 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126 126>,
+								/bits/ 8 <2 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60 60>;
+							paths-cck = /bits/ 8 <48 42 42 42 42>;
+							paths-ofdm = /bits/ 8 <42 36 36 36 36>;
+							paths-ofdm-bf = /bits/ 8 <36 36 36 36>;
